Step 1: Create a Web Forms Project Open Visual Studio 2019.
Create ASP.NET Web Application (.NET Framework). Select Web Forms.
Add the following files:
Web.sitemap Default.aspx Page2.aspx Page3.aspx Page4.aspx
Step 1
Add Site Map file
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<siteMap xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/AspNet/SiteMap-File-1.0">
<siteMapNode url="pract5a.aspx" title="Home"
description="Home page of our website">
<siteMapNode url="clsProp.aspx" title="Page2" description="Page2" />
<siteMapNode url="Default3.aspx" title="Page3" description="Page3" />
<siteMapNode url="Default2.aspx" title="Page4" description="Page4" />
</siteMapNode>
</siteMap> Step2:
Add SiteMapDataSource control and Menu control from toolbox to the page
Step3:
Pract5a.aspx
<%@ Page Language="C#" AutoEventWireup="true" CodeBehind="pract5a.aspx.cs" Inherits="practical5a.WebForm1" %>
<!DOCTYPE html>
 
<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
<head runat="server">
<title>Home</title>
</head>
<body>
<form id="form1" runat="server">
<div>
<asp:Label ID="Label1" runat="server" Text="Home"></asp:Label>
<br /><br />
<asp:Menu ID="Menu1" runat="server" DataSourceID="SiteMapDataSource1">
</asp:Menu>
<br />
<asp:SiteMapDataSource ID="SiteMapDataSource1" runat="server">
</asp:SiteMapDataSource>
</div>
</form>
</body>
</html>
